# Phase 3G: first playable browser build

The original C++ handheld game now runs natively on the Ubuntu NUC behind the private authenticated server. The browser displays its actual 240×240 pixels and sends virtual handheld inputs. The first playable composition has one controlling participant per server process.

## Verified gameplay

An interactive browser session on the Windows PC used a private SSH local forward to the real NUC server. It completed the original title, Fighter/Blades selection, rolled statistics, acceptance, town, real generated dungeon, tile movement, door transition, monster awareness, initiative, original combat menus and attacks. A melee attack displayed **Goblin Archer takes 7 damage**. The encounter ended with **Victory! You gain 135 XP.** The character then moved again and reopened the original menus. The character sheet showed **135/2000 XP and 4/9 HP**. These values came from the production runtime; no browser dice, HP assignment, position authority or combat simulation exists.

The same complete production playthrough also passes automatically on Windows and Ubuntu. Tests issue only virtual handheld inputs, inspect production state and verify wall collision, long press, generated monsters, HP damage on both sides, combat completion and subsequent exploration. Seed 2 supplies the documented reproducible test route; other seeds retain genuine generated encounters and defeat is possible.

